I'm not sure it's an issue of play balance for Nethack to have larger
mazes.  Would it make the game earier or harder to have larger levels?
 More rooms means more items earlier, but also more monsters generated
at the start of a level.  The only definite effect I can see would be
that it'd take more turns to explore a level, meaning food would be
more important.

Even if the game got easier or harder by increasing the size of
dungeon levels, it'd be the sort of thing that could be compensated
for by merely making items, monsters and features more or less common.
 Their frequencies are variables approximately as arbitrary as level
size.

